  <h2>From the manuscript</h2>

  <p><em>Go to Hell</em></p>

  <p id="introduction"><em>Introduction</em></p>

  <p>We hope you will not be offended by the title "Please Go to Hell." It is neither a directive or invitation but, rather, a forewarning that if you read it, in entirety, it is very likely your ticket to hell has been punched and you will join us as soon as the vacancy committee finds a place for you and your particular talents. Hell is a pretty exclusive club, we have learned, and we were turned away several times until we returned with the proper credentials and references.</p>

  <p>Thundermug Jackson had been told to go to hell by the dregs of humanity to, and including, the most influential people he had met in his journeys. Some even put special emphasis on the command by adding "go straight to hell." There is no straight path to hell. It is a circuitous trail, not clearly marked, and forks to dead ends that test one's endurance. Those persons with the proper attitude, qualified and deserving, will have few problems.</p>

  <p>Let us tell you, it doesn't get any better than this. We laugh at ourselves, we laugh at our neighbors and we don't sue McDonald's because their coffee is too hot or because their high calorie food makes us fat. In fact, we don't sue anybody. Lawyers who found their way to us liked our lifestyle so much they begged to stay and have either become bartenders or janitors.</p>

  <p>Hell is a separate and sovereign colony not dependent on any governing body because everyone here is equal. We haven't determined equal to what, but that is the least of our worries. We should add that Hell is like any spirited community and you will find a certain faction that believes it is more equal than the rest of us, but since we have no specific entity or object to be equal to there is really no social difference.</p>

  <p>We don't know where the hell we're going or why, but we intend to raise hell and put a chunk under it.</p>

  <p id="prologue-to-the-preface"><em>Prologue to the Preface</em></p>

  <p><em>"Hey there, don't skip this page. If you want to go hell, you must read all of the publication regardless of its contents or how boring it may seem."</em></p>

  <p>Before you turn another page, however, be advised that the authors are not writers, per se. We are mentally unstable due to many and varied factors and grossly uninhibited in our advanced years. Pauline Roberta Jackson Bates, known affectionately as "Bubbles," has a degree from a prestigious college that qualifies her as a learned person and capable of writing real novels. Her ambitions along that line were rudely interrupted when she was kidnapped by aliens from a distant galaxy just after graduation. She was returned with a vast knowledge of the universe and interstellar travel but her brain was wiped clean of prior academic learning. My credentials are far less noteworthy, though I have exposed my instability and incompetence in other publications that were well received in Latvia, where a friend on missionary work shared them with students in his classes. They couldn't read them, but they liked the illustrations.</p>

  <p>In our immediate family, Bubbles and I have outlasted the other players and share a common bond in spite of our disparate mental abilities. Our goal, in this publication, is to jog memories of oldsters and acquaint others with short stories of a variety of people who influenced us, one way or another, and gave the mining town of Creede the aura and flavor that pervades to this day and draws the curious into its fold. The hell raisers are gone and "good riddance" to us. It is time for a new and invigorating culture to polish Creede's image and attract artisans who will preserve the past but take the town to a new and higher level.</p>

  <p>I, personally, am well acquainted with the landlord in Hell and rest assured I will provide references for each and every one of you who wish a change of scenery and atmosphere after reading our stories. We will inject a few previously unpublished poems and a few previously unpublished thoughts that probably should have remained unpublished.</p>

  <p id="preface-to-the-foreword"><em>Preface to the Foreword</em></p>

  <p><em>Why are sisters smarter than brothers?<br>
  And their combined intellect less than Mothers?</em></p>

  <p>My brothers and I weren't prepared for a sister. Especially a sister with a brain that absorbed as much in her first six years as our brains absorbed in twelve years or more. We sprang from the same loins, nurtured in the same womb and nursed from the same breast but somewhere along the genetic trail, between our births and hers, the DNA spiral was altered with smarter genes.</p>

  <p>Girls are smarter than boys. Boys are smarter than their fathers until they partially mature at twenty years of age to find their old dads, in a surprising surge of aptitude, surpassed them in scholarly capabilities and common sense. Through it all the mothers sit back and let us all make fools of ourselves, then rescue us from total failure with both superior intellect and love.</p>

  <p>Mothers are a national treasure and we darned well better appreciate them and make their lives a little easier.</p>

  <p id="foreword"><em>Foreword</em></p>

  <p>Okays, we got a little carried away with a prologue, a preface and now a foreword, which are basically the same in meaning but we felt if we could confuse you enough at the start we could fake the rest of it and you wouldn't be too critical of the conflaberration we dreamed up to gain a little fame or grease the skids for a faster ride to hell than the leisurely pace reserved for the elderly. The word "conflaberration" is not in the dictionary. It combines a few words or parts of words that, if assembled correctly, would amount to a confession for misleading you.</p>

  <p>Some people write books for a living, they are creative and put a story together that can be sold for a profit. Some people write books because they feel they have knowledge to pass on to those less learned. We write to embarrass family members in hopes the most prominent and well-heeled will offer to buy the manuscript before it reaches a publisher. Unfortunately, we have no prominent or well-heeled family members and the only offer we have received to date is not suitable for printing and contains threats of bodily harm if the manuscript is not destroyed.</p>

  <p>We do not take kindly to threats and we shall not be deterred. Family secrets should be aired before the skeletons in the closet gather cobwebs and dust. Our advice to family members is to brace yourselves as firmly as possible and deny any relationship.</p>

  <p>I always write with fear and trepidation. I don't know what trepidation means but it sounds scholarly and, above all, I want to sound scholarly conflaberrating with my sister since she has a college degree and has traveled in space with a superior, alien race. With her background, she has no fear of anything on Earth.</p>

  <p>The main purpose of our conspiracy is to let you know that Creede was and is a very special place. The road to everywhere starts right in Creede, Colorado. If you are so inclined, the stories may serve as a guideline for the journey to hell and you are encouraged to read on. If you are not so inclined, the stories and poetry may offer you a guideline to avoid the journey, but "nothing ventured, nothing gained" Please read on.</p>
</section>
